{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/485751-re-rolling-disciplines","id":485751,"title":"Re-Rolling Disciplines","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-04-19T15:07:20-07:00","id":485751,"title":"Re-Rolling Disciplines","content":"I can't find anything specific in the books, so I'm guessing that a vampire with Majesty going for Confidante or Dominate going for Mesmerise can keep re-rolling each turn until successful? Maybe with a cumulative -1 penalty to each roll? Certainly makes a high resistance far more uncertain when they can keep going. Naturally someone repeatedly trying to Mesmerise a person will come off as weird and creepy, especially if you do the supernatural flashes to give a sense of the Beast trying but failing to succeed, though Confidante's attempts would theoretically be subtle enough that you get as many attempts as you have a dice pool to get it off.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My horror roleplaying blog with a strong focus on World of Darkness and Call of Cthulhu can be found here: <a href=\"http://stwildonroleplaying.blogspot.com.au/\" target=\"_blank\">http://stwildonroleplaying.blogspot.com.au/</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1248-laraqua","name":"Laraqua","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-19T17:04:36-07:00","id":485842,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>V:tR 2e, page 173</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Successive Attempts: When you fail a roll, you may be able to try again. If time is not an issue and your character is under no pressure to perform, you may make successive attempts with your full dice pool. In the far more likely situation that time is short and the situation is tense, each subsequent attempt has a cumulative \u20131 die penalty \u2014 so the third time a character tries to break down the door that\u2019s keeping her inside a burning building, her roll has a \u20132 die penalty. Successive attempts do not apply to extended actions.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd use the above rules. For Mesmerize, I'd personally almost exclusively go for the dice penalty, since making eye contact gets creepy, and it'd be justified for the ST to just have the NPC up and leave after being freaked out enough. Confidante can go either way. Majesty seems to be the subtle scalpel to Dominate's sledgehammer, and it works by making people want to help you rather than controlling them. Majesty is less overt than Dominate, so I'd say it could go either way. That's just how I'd reason it out, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-20T02:20:12-07:00","id":486155,"title":"","content":"I apple a cumulative -1 penalty for situations like this. And goddamnit, I totally forgot the supernatural flares upon fails... Which I did try to get into the game previously. That idea/thing is so underdeveloped in the book :/","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-20T06:51:05-07:00","id":486293,"title":"","content":"Just throwing this in there. for Confidant you have to be awed first which means they already want to be around you/ look at you ect. so I wouldnt apply a penalty for getting creepy like dominate. though in certain situations with Dominate if you are both parties are having a stare down/trying to intimidate each other. I wouldnt apply the penalty there. Take it as a case by case.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-21T17:03:37-07:00","id":487802,"title":"","content":"Hmm, I may go with the cumulative -1 penalties as a general rule in LARP because being able to roll 20 times until you get a success just by preventing the other PC to leave would likely grate on all the players - can foresee even the users of such powers thinking that's broken. In Tabletop, I'll keep it for things like when there's a time crunch or like with Dominate where the Dominator might start getting self-conscious and worried as the werewolf gets antsy under those demanding (and thus far ineffective) commands.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My horror roleplaying blog with a strong focus on World of Darkness and Call of Cthulhu can be found here: <a href=\"http://stwildonroleplaying.blogspot.com.au/\" target=\"_blank\">http://stwildonroleplaying.blogspot.com.au/</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1248-laraqua","name":"Laraqua","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}